WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.240
Give a young mammal extra nerve growth factor, and its sympathetic ganglia swell.

2
00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:15.460
Inject a newborn mouse with an antiserum against it, and the ganglia waste away.

3
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.460
Call the protein NGF.

4
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:22.300
Results like these tempt a strong conclusion.

5
00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.780
Does NGF decide how many neurons an animal has?

6
00:00:27.683 --> 00:00:30.823
A small ganglion can mean two things.

7
00:00:31.503 --> 00:00:37.303
Either too few neurons were made, or the normal number was made and some were lost.

8
00:00:38.583 --> 00:00:43.603
In chick spinal ganglia, many neurons formed and grew fibres first.

9
00:00:44.863 --> 00:00:47.003
Dying cells became conspicuous later.

10
00:00:48.163 --> 00:00:49.623
Neurons are overproduced.

11
00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:55.117
The target is the tissue an axon grows to and connects with.

12
00:00:55.537 --> 00:00:58.357
It supplies the factor, and the amount is limited.

13
00:00:59.457 --> 00:01:01.577
Axons that reach the target take it up.

14
00:01:02.277 --> 00:01:05.097
Neurons that get too little die by apoptosis.

15
00:01:06.177 --> 00:01:09.857
The idea is that neurons compete for a limiting amount of factor.

16
00:01:10.597 --> 00:01:13.717
Death should come when axons reach the target, not before.

17
00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:16.890
An antiserum carries a doubt.

18
00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:21.270
It might kill neurons by binding something other than NGF.

19
00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:24.190
A knockout mouse settles it.

20
00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:30.870
Mice lacking a working TrkA, the receptor for NGF, still form the ganglion.

21
00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:35.050
Neurons are made and their axons start to grow as usual.

22
00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:40.490
But the sympathetic neurons are lost after embryonic day 15.5.

23
00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:42.810
The neurons were produced.

24
00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:44.990
What failed was survival.

25
00:01:45.883 --> 00:01:49.943
Now add excess NGF to a developing chick embryo.

26
00:01:50.943 --> 00:01:55.883
The ganglia get larger, because more of the neurons that were made escape the normal

27
00:01:55.883 --> 00:01:58.923
death. How would you know it is survival?

28
00:02:00.003 --> 00:02:04.983
You count neurons and dying cells across the death period, and you mark dividing

29
00:02:04.983 --> 00:02:12.343
cells. No new neurons appear from nothing, and no neuron changes what kind of neuron it is.

31
00:02:12.617 --> 00:02:14.137
This gives a ceiling.

32
00:02:15.157 --> 00:02:20.637
Neurons surviving equal the smaller of two numbers: the neurons made, and the

33
00:02:20.637 --> 00:02:22.277
neurons the factor can support.

34
00:02:23.257 --> 00:02:25.457
Extra factor raises the second number.

35
00:02:26.057 --> 00:02:28.777
Nothing about a survival factor raises the first.

36
00:02:29.417 --> 00:02:33.537
The ceiling holds for the population you measured, with its own factor.

37
00:02:34.317 --> 00:02:38.577
A survival factor can decide how many of the neurons made stay alive.

38
00:02:38.577 --> 00:02:41.437
It cannot add neurons that were never made.
